+// V15 compute hazard tracker (KYTY_SYNC_COMPUTE=3/4). Compute writes (bound storage buffers with
+// their guest ranges, storage images, BDA writes incl. writes through the BDA page table) of the
+// last 64 dispatches are remembered. A later dispatch/draw that reads an overlapping range, any
+// image after an image write, or any memory through BDA after a range/BDA write is reported once
+// per (producer, consumer) pair as a [V15] compute hazard line with the real ranges. These are
+// already ordered on the GPU by the per-dispatch COMPUTE -> ALL_COMMANDS barrier (one VkQueue,
+// one command stream), so the report is diagnostic; KYTY_HAZARD_COMPUTE_BARRIER=1 additionally
+// emits an explicit global barrier at each hit.
+void HazardNoteComputeWrites(const ShaderStageRuntime& runtime);
+// Returns true when a hit was found (and a barrier was emitted, if enabled).
+bool HazardCheckComputeReaders(vk::CommandBuffer vk_buffer, const ShaderStageRuntime& runtime,
+                               const char* consumer_kind, uint64_t extra_address,
+                               uint64_t extra_size);
